s exported `id`. For npm plugins, it is the exported `id` or the package name if `id` is omitted.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:37:- Plugins are enabled by default. `plugin_enabled` is only for explicit overrides, usually to disable a plugin with `false`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:38:- `plugin_enabled` is merged across config layers.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:39:- Runtime enable/disable state is also stored in KV under `plugin_enabled`; that KV state overrides config on startup.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:45:- Import types from `@opencode-ai/plugin/tui`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:46:- `@opencode-ai/plugin` exports `./tui` and declares optional peer deps on `@opentui/core` and `@opentui/solid`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:52:import type { TuiPlugin, TuiPluginModule } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin/tui\"\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:55:  api.command.register(() => [\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:75:const plugin: TuiPluginModule & { id: string } = {\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:80:export default plugin\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:90:- `package.json` `main` is only used for server plugin entrypoint resolution.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:92:- File/path plugins must export a non-empty `id`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:93:- npm plugins may omit `id`; package `name` is used.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:94:- Runtime identity is the resolved plugin id. Later plugins with the same id are rejected, including collisions with internal plugin ids.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:97:- Legacy compatibility: path specs like `./plugin` can resolve to `./plugin/index.ts` (or `index.js`) when `package.json` is missing.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:98:- The `./plugin -> ./plugin/index.*` fallback applies to both server and TUI v1 loading.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:99:- There is no directory auto-discovery for TUI plugins; they must be listed in `tui.json`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:103:Package manifest is read from `package.json` field `oc-plugin`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:109:  \"name\": \"@acme/opencode-plugin\",\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:115:  \"oc-plugin\": [\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:124:npm plugins can declare a version compatibility range in `package.json` using the standard `engines` field:\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:135:- If the range is not satisfied, the plugin is skipped with a warning and a session error.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:137:- File plugins are never checked; only npm package plugins are validated.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:139:- Install flow is shared by CLI and TUI in `src/plugin/install.ts`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:141:- `opencode plugin <module>` and TUI install both run install → manifest read → config patch.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:148:- `patchPluginConfig` returns structured result unions (`ok`, `code`, fields by error kind) instead of custom thrown errors.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:150:- `patchPluginConfig` uses targeted `jsonc-parser` edits, so existing JSONC comments are preserved when plugin entries are added or replaced.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:153:- Tuple targets in `oc-plugin` provide default options written into config.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:156:- There is no uninstall, list, or update CLI command for external plugins.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:157:- Local file plugins are configured directly in `tui.json`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:159:When `plugin` entries exist in a writable `.opencode` dir or `OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR`, OpenCode installs `@opencode-ai/plugin` into that dir and writes:\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:166:That is what makes local config-scoped plugins able to import `@opencode-ai/plugin/tui`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:168:## TUI plugin API\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:173:- `api.command.register(cb)` / `api.command.trigger(value)`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:184:- `api.slots.register(plugin)`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:185:- `api.plugins.list()`, `activate(id)`, `deactivate(id)`, `add(spec)`, `install(spec, options?)`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:190:`api.command.register` returns an unregister function. Command rows support:\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:203:- Hidden commands are removed from the command dialog and slash list, but still respond to keybinds and `command.trigger(value)` if `enabled !== false`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:208:- Any other name is treated as a plugin route.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:214:- If multiple plugins register the same route name, the last registered route wins.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:215:- Unknown plugin routes render a fallback screen with a `go home` action.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:232:- `api.keybind.create(defaults, overrides?)` builds a plugin-local keybind set.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:238:- `api.kv` is the shared app KV store backed by `state/kv.json`. It is not plugin-namespaced.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:253:  - `session.permission(sessionID)`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:276:- Relative theme paths are resolved from the plugin root.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:279:- If the theme name already exists, install is skipped unless plugin metadata state is `updated`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:280:- On `updated`, host only rewrites themes previously tracked for that plugin and only when source `mtime`/`size` changed.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:281:- Local plugins persist installed themes under the local `.opencode/themes` area near the plugin config source.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:282:- Global plugins persist installed themes under the global `themes` dir.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:300:- `api.slots.register(plugin)` returns the host-assigned slot plugin id.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:301:- `api.slots.register(plugin)` does not return an unregister function.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:302:- Returned ids are `pluginId`, `pluginId:1`, `pluginId:2`, and so on.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:309:- `api.plugins.list()` returns `{ id, source, spec, target, enabled, active }[]`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:310:- `enabled` is the persisted desired state. `active` means the plugin is currently initialized.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:311:- `api.plugins.activate(id)` sets `enabled=true`, persists it into KV, and initializes the plugin.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:312:- `api.plugins.deactivate(id)` sets `enabled=false`, persists it into KV, and disposes the plugin scope.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:313:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` trims the input and returns `false` for an empty string.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:314:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` treats the input as the runtime plugin spec and loads it without re-reading `tui.json`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:315:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` no-ops when that resolved spec (or resolved plugin id) is already loaded.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:316:- `api.plugins.add(spec)` assumes enabled and always attempts initialization (it does not consult config/KV enable state).\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:317:- `api.plugins.install(spec, { global? })` runs install -> manifest read -> config patch using the same helper flow as CLI install.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:318:- `api.plugins.install(...)` returns either `{ ok: false, message, missing? }` or `{ ok: true, dir, tui }`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:319:- `api.plugins.install(...)` does not load plugins into the current session. Call `api.plugins.add(spec)` to load after install.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:320:- For packages that declare a tuple `tui` target in `oc-plugin`, `api.plugins.install(...)` stages those tuple options so a following `api.plugins.add(spec)` uses them.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:321:- If activation fails, the plugin can remain `enabled=true` and `active=false`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:335:Metadata is persisted by plugin id.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:337:- File plugin fingerprint is `target|modified`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:338:- npm plugin fingerprint is `target|requested|version`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:339:- Internal plugins get synthetic metadata with `state: \"same\"`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:343:- Internal TUI plugins load first.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:344:- External TUI plugins load from `tuiConfig.plugin`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:345:- `--pure` / `OPENCODE_PURE` skips external TUI plugins only.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:346:- External plugin resolution and import are parallel.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:347:- External plugin activation is sequential to keep command, route, and side-effect order deterministic.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:348:- File plugins that fail initially are retried once after waiting for config dependency installation.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:349:- Runtime add uses the same external loader path, including the file-plugin retry after dependency wait.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:352:- Plugin init failure rolls back that plugin's tracked registrations and loading continues.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:354:  - command registrations\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:361:- Total cleanup budget per plugin is 5 seconds; timeout/error is logged and shutdown continues.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:363:## Built-in plugins\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:372:- `internal:plugin-manager`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:376:The plugin manager is exposed as a command with title `Plugins` and value `plugins.list`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:378:- Keybind name is `plugin_manager`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:380:- It lists both internal and external plugins.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:383:- It also exposes command `plugins.install` with title `Install plugin`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:388:- Manager install uses `api.plugins.install(spec, { global })`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:390:- If install reports `tui=true`, manager then calls `api.plugins.add(spec)`.\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:395:- Local smoke plugin: `.opencode/plugins/tui-smoke.tsx`\npackages/opencode/specs/tui-plugins.md:397:- Local smoke theme: `.opencode/plugins/smoke-theme.json`\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:11:import { Plugin } from \"@/plugin\"\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:12:import { PtyID } from \"./schema\"\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:62:      command: z.string(),\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:73:    command: z.string().optional(),\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:177:          const command = input.command || Shell.preferred()\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:179:          if (Shell.login(command)) {\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:198:          log.info(\"creating session\", { id, cmd: command, args, cwd })\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:201:          const proc = spawn(command, args, {\npackages/opencode/src/pty/index.ts:210:            command,\npackages/opencode/migration/20260312043431_session_message_cursor/snapshot.json:36:      \"name\": \"permission\",\npackages/opencode/migration/20260312043431_session_message_cursor/snapshot.json:417:      \"name\": \"commands\",\npackages/opencode/migration/20260312043431_session_message_cursor/snapshot.json:539:      \"table\": \"permiss